            <remarks>This class is used by the <see cref="T:MonetaryTransactionRequest" /> class.</remarks>
            <tocexclude />]]></xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="EntityAttribute" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The value of this tag defines the value to be inserted into CASHBOXTXNENTITYATTRIB table for attribute defined in EntityAttributeCode. The value provided must be valid for the EntityAttribCd. The value will be saved only when the tag has valid non-empty contents. 
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="EntityAttributeCode" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            EntityAttributeCode attribute identifies the type of entity attribute to add to the CashboxTxnEntityAttrib table. Valid values are stored in the EntityAttrib Table. The entityAttribCd must be defined in EntityTypEntityAttrib for EntityTypCd = ‘CTXN’.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="CashboxTxnEntityAttribute" nillable="true" type="tns:CashboxTxnEntityAttribute"/>
  <xs:complexType name="CheckIssue">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:appinfo/>
      <xs:documentation><![CDATA[<summary>
            Required information for official check transactions.
            </summary>
            <remarks>This class is used by the <see cref="T:MonetaryTransactionRequest" /> class.</remarks>
            <tocexclude />]]></xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="CheckNumber" nillable="true" type="xs:long">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Check Number assigned to the Official Check. Check numbers can only be supplied 
            when the status attribute on the CheckIssue node has been set to ―PRT. 
            If CheckNbr is provided, it must be greater or equal to the account's next check number. 
            When a check number is not sent and the status has been set to ―PRT,
            the system will generate a valid check number and report it in the response. 
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="IsPayableToAny" nillable="true" type="xs:boolean">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            A Y/N value to indicate if the check is payable to all or either of the payees.
            This is required only multiple payees information is provided.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="Memo" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Memo text for the Official Check.The maximum length of a Memo is 254,
            but that is also subject to what can fit on the check.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="Payee" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Payee for the Official Check.
            Maximum length of 60 characters
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="PayeeAddress" nillable="true" type="tns:PayeeAddress">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Wrapper tag containing payee address information.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="PayeesInfo" nillable="true" type="tns:ArrayOfPayeeInfo">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            A collection of one or more payees to be created for this check.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="Status" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Attribute identifies the current status of the Official Check.
            Valid status codes for Check Issues are ASGN – Assigned to Teller and PRT – Printed.
            All Check Issue transactions sent in a single Transaction Root Node, with the ASGN status, 
            will be grouped in the same Batch Check Print Queue that has been linked to the same Parent/Reference Account number for the check. 
            The Parent/Reference Account number will be derived from the ParentReqNbr tag for each Check Issue transaction request.
            All Check Issue transactions sent in a single Transaction Root Node, with the PRT status will be places in individual Batch Check Print Queues.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="CheckIssue" nillable="true" type="tns:CheckIssue"/>
  <xs:complexType name="PayeeAddress">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:appinfo/>
      <xs:documentation><![CDATA[<summary>
            Contains payee address information.
            </summary>
            <remarks>This class is used by the <see cref="T:CheckIssue" /> class.</remarks>
            <tocexclude />]]></xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="Addresslines" nillable="true" type="tns:ArrayOfAddressLineInformation">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Wrapper tag that identifies multiple address lines.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="CensusTractNumber" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Census Tract Number from the Census Bureau.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="CityName" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The city name of the address. This is a Required Tag.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="CountryCode" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Attribute identifies the country code, e.g., USA. 
            Valid values are defined by CTRY table. Default value is USA. 
            This attribute is required when sending an address.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="CountrySubDivisionCode" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Country Subdivision Code is used to identify the subdivision of a country.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="MailCode" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The country mail code for non-U.S. addresses.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="SMSANumber" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Metropolitan Statistical Number for this address.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="State" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The state code for the address. Valid values are defined by STATE table.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="ZipCode" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The 5-digit ZIP code of the address.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="ZipSuffix" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The 4-digit ZIP code suffix of the address.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="PayeeAddress" nillable="true" type="tns:PayeeAddress"/>
  <xs:complexType name="ArrayOfAddressLineInformation">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" name="AddressLineInformation" nillable="true" type="tns:AddressLineInformation"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="ArrayOfAddressLineInformation" nillable="true" type="tns:ArrayOfAddressLineInformation"/>
  <xs:complexType name="AddressLineInformation">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:appinfo/>
      <xs:documentation><![CDATA[<summary>
            A specific address line for a payee address.
            </summary>
            <remarks>This class is used by the <see cref="T:PayeeAddress" /> class.</remarks>
            <tocexclude />]]></xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="AddressLineText" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The address line text, e.g., 805 South St.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="AddressLineTypeCode" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Attribute indicates the address line type, e.g., ST = Street, APTN = Apartment. 
            Valid values are defined by ADDRLINETYP table. This attribute is required when sending an address
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="AddressLineInformation" nillable="true" type="tns:AddressLineInformation"/>
  <xs:complexType name="ArrayOfPayeeInfo">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" name="PayeeInfo" nillable="true" type="tns:PayeeInfo"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="ArrayOfPayeeInfo" nillable="true" type="tns:ArrayOfPayeeInfo"/>
  <xs:complexType name="PayeeInfo">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:appinfo/>
      <xs:documentation><![CDATA[<summary>
            Repeating node used for inserting rows in the AcctBankCheckPayee table.
            </summary>
            <remarks>This class is used by the <see cref="T:CheckIssue" /> class.</remarks>
            <tocexclude />]]></xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="FirstName" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The First Name specifies what the first name of this payee was at the time 
            this check was issued, when this payee is a person.
            Maximum length of 20 characters
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="LastName" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Last Name specifies what the last name of this payee was at the time this 
            check was issued, when this payee is a person.
            Maximum length of 20 characters
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="MiddleName" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Middle Name specifies what the middle name of this payee was at the time 
            this check was issued, when this payee is a person.
            Maximum length of 20 characters
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="OrganizationName" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Organization Name specifies what the name of this payee was at the time 
            this check was issued, when this payee is an organization.
            Maximum length of 60 characters
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="PayeeOrganizationNumber" nillable="true" type="xs:long">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Payee Organization Number uniquely identifies this payee on the check, 
            when this payee is an organization that has been established in the database.
            Even if the payee name entered does not match the one stored in DNA for the 
            OrgNbr entered, entered data will be saved as it is. 
            Maximum length of 22 numeric
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="PayeePersonNumber" nillable="true" type="xs:long">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Payee Person Number uniquely identifies this payee on the check, 
            when this payee is a person who has been established in the database.
            Even if the payee name entered does not match the one stored in DNA 
            for the PersNbr entered, entered data will be saved as it is.
            Maximum length of 22 numeric
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="SalutationCode" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Salutation Code uniquely identifies the standard salutation that was in use 
            for this payee at the time this check was issued, when this payee is a person.
            Valid values are defined by SALU table.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="Suffix" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:appinfo/>
          <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The Suffix specifies any suffix that was applied to the name of this payee 
            at the time this check was issued, when this payee is a person.
            Maximum length of 10 characters
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="PayeeInfo" nillable="true" type="tns:PayeeInfo"/>
